% =============================================================================
% fill — μMALL Intuitionistic Linear Logic (TODO_0009 rungs 2-3, Baelde 2012)
% =============================================================================
%
% ILL + least/greatest fixed points (μ/ν) — the inductive/coinductive frontier
% (cyclic proofs, coinduction, the μMALL exponential subsumption THY_0042).
%
% The surface is INHERITED, not copied: @extends ill (the meta-parser's
% loadChain merges ILL's connective table), so fill declares only the fill-OWN
% fixpoint connectives below. Keeping μMALL out of production ILL is a
% deliberate FIREWALL: ILL declares no @category fixpoint, so deriveRoles()
% yields no roles.lfp/roles.gfp and the generic cyclic-proof engine
% (bridge.js / gtc-check.js / focused.js) stays dormant on the EVM proof path
% — no extra fixpoint rules in ILL's backward fragment, no μ/ν rejection cost
% in the lax-monad bridge. A μMALL change cannot regress an EVM proof.
%
% The kernel mu/nu TAGS (store.js) stay global binder vocabulary, like
% exists/forall — a tag existing in the kernel table is not "ILL using it";
% only the @category declaration below binds them into a calculus's grammar
% and roles. The four unfold rules live in fill.rules.
% =============================================================================

@extends ill.

% Least fixed point: μX.B(X) — inductive data (Nat = μX. I + X, List, Tree).
% Unary binder (body de-Bruijn-encoded, like ∃/∀); X is the recursion variable.
% Polarity: positive (μL invertible / eager, μR needs focus) — must be declared
% explicitly: the single-premise unfold rule's 'preserved' context flow would
% otherwise infer negative.
mu: formula -> formula
  @ascii "mu _"
  @latex "\\mu #1"
  @prec 45 right
  @category fixpoint
  @polarity positive.

% Greatest fixed point: νX.B(X) — coinductive data (Stream = νX. A * X,
% Signal = νX. A & X = !A). Polarity: negative (νR invertible / eager, νL needs
% focus). De Morgan dual of μ.
nu: formula -> formula
  @ascii "nu _"
  @latex "\\nu #1"
  @prec 45 right
  @category fixpoint
  @polarity negative.
